          </p>

          <p>
            There are two caveats worth knowing. First, the published samples are Pure Chocho; the testing page does not show a separate panel for Vanilla, Cacao or Horchata, which add cacao (a known lead and cadmium source in chocolate products generally) and other ingredients. Second, the product page still carries a California Prop 65 warning for lead. Brands often print that warning as legal protection regardless of results, so it is not evidence of a problem, but it is on the listing.
